  "slug": "zero-dna-mirrordna-8a09",
  "summary": "Recent preprints tokenize structures, DNA and nanopore signal, while RNA models add structural guidance and stratified benchmarks for generalization.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is learned discretization or structure-aware representation as a basis for biomolecular foundation models. The all-atom structure tokenizer compresses geometry into discrete tokens, Brieno applies residual vector quantization to raw nanopore signal, and MirrorDNA learns a tokenizer that enforces reverse-complement symmetry in a compact DNA model. The RNA-focused items differ in approach: structRFM pretrains on 21M sequence-structure pairs with new benchmarks, and TriTower-m6Am fuses semantic, sequential and structural towers for m6Am site prediction. RPFace emphasizes benchmark bias and generalization in protein-RNA interface prediction using a small sequence-only model. What is new is the move from fixed encodings toward tokenizers that embed modality-specific symmetries, with generalization testing increasingly emphasized.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-09"
}
